From 69628c3257fd72abc3060e534f8001f0264acaaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivela=CC=88?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 13:39:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] extensions: offer the notifications namespace

1Password registers notifications.onClicked and onButtonClicked at the
top level of its worker. The namespace was absent, so the worker threw
on its first line and never started: "Service worker registration
failed. Status code: 15". It calls create, update, clear and getAll
besides, so declaring the events alone would only move the failure to
the first thing it wanted to say.

A notification an extension asks for is a notification. It goes where a
page's goes, to the application, as a UserNotificationController through
the profile adapter's clients, so an application that already shows one
shows this one and the reader is not asked to tell them apart. The
reader's answer comes back the same way: a click is
notifications.onClicked and a close is onClosed.

What an application can show is a title, a message and an origin, so
buttons, images and progress are read and not passed on, and
onButtonClicked is declared and never raised. getPermissionLevel is
nocompile: there is no level to report and the extensions layer has no
histogram value for the call.

The registry gives each notification an id of its own, so two profiles
running the same extension do not collide on a name either of them
chose, and drops what an extension that is no longer enabled was
showing. At context teardown its notifications are dropped rather than
closed: that runs inside ~ProfileQt, and the adapter the close would
reach through is already going.
